<title>GERMANY: Viag to retain its Vereinsbank stake.</title>
<headline>Viag to retain its Vereinsbank stake.</headline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>German diversified utility Viag AG said on Monday that it would retain its holdings in the Bavarian bank Bayerische Vereinsbank, due to merge with Bayerische Hypo-Bank.</p>
<p>&quot;The shareholding is a valuable investment and is not to be viewed as a strategic option,&quot; a spokesman told Reuters. Viag owns 10.24 percent of Vereinsbank through its Bayernwerk unit.</p>
<p>Vereinsbank announced the merger on Monday, which will result in Germany's second largest bank group if the merger receives regulatory approval.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
